        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Foundation and arc row" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Chain a multiple of 10 plus 3. Row 1: dc in each ch to end. Row 2: *ch 5, skip 4 dc, dc in next dc; repeat from * across." }]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pineapple rows (rows 3 to 9)" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Row 3: work 9 tr into each ch-5 arc (pineapple base). Row 4: ch 4, *tr in each tr of the pineapple separated by ch 1 (9 separated trebles). Row 5: ch 4, tr in each of 8 gaps (8 tr). Rows 6 to 9: continue decreasing by 1 treble each row. Final row: 1 tr left, ch 3, sl st to form the tip picot. Fasten off." }]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Attaching" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Sew the foundation row to the fabric edge with the tapestry needle. Weave in the ends." }]
      }
    ]
